# GitHub Issues and PRs

Read `AGENTS.md` §13 **GitHub Issue Structure** for the full rule.

## When creating issues (`/speckit-taskstoissues`)

- One **epic** per spec; one **sub-issue** per phase/user story in `tasks.md`
- Tasks (`T001`, …) are checkboxes inside sub-issue bodies — never standalone issues
- Write `specs/<feature>/github-issues.md` with all issue numbers and a **PR closing keywords** block

## When creating an implementation PR

1. Read `specs/<feature>/github-issues.md`
2. Include an **Issues closed** section with `Closes #NNN` for the epic **and every sub-issue**
3. Use `.github/pull_request_template.md` as the starting structure

Do not close only the epic. Sub-issues do not auto-close when the parent closes.
